{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493091-mystery-of-the-blood-2e-homebrew","id":1493091,"title":"Mystery of the Blood [2e Homebrew]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-14T19:12:57-07:00","id":1493091,"title":"Mystery of the Blood [2e Homebrew]","content":"Another one for the batch. I hope you guys enjoy. I know that many people already portted this old Coil from 1st edition, but I wanted to add my insights and changes to it.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mystery of the Blood</span></b><br /> The scholars of the Voivode study the power of the Vitae over bonds and progeny, but those of the Mystery of the Blood ponder about the nature of Vitae itself. For them, Vitae is as much of a blessing as it is a curse. Initiates of the Mystery believe that by overcoming the need for Vitae a Dragon can finally use it as it should be, a weapon and not a hindrance. So far, the studies have wielded great results, but not yet to the point where the Kindred will let go of their need for blood.<br /> <br /> Scales of the Blood can strength the Vitae of the Dragon, allowing him to wake up torpid Kindreds and to preserve blood outside a living vessel for later consumption, allowing for extended periods of fasting in attempts to master the need for blood. Extended periods of fasting, consumption of blood beyond the capacity of the body, hunger induced frenzy are common practices. The aim is to understand at what lengths the Dragon\u2019s body is controlled by Vitae. For when Vitae is only a fuel for the Disciplines and powers and not a dire necessity, the next step into the evolution can be taken.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Coil of the Blood</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Blood Bank</b> \u2022<br /> A Dragon\u2019s need for blood begins no differently than that of others of his kind. Though he still requires Vitae, he has discovered a way to harbor more of it. The Dragon can store a number of additional Vitae equal to half his Coil of the Blood rating, rounded up. The player also adds his Coil of the Blood rating to his &quot;Starting Vitae&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Seeps Slowly</b> \u2022\u2022<br /> With a newfound understanding of his Vitae, the Dragon can better animate his body. He now only needs to spend Vitae to awaken once every number of days equal to his Coil of the Blood rating. However, if he wishes to awaken during the day, he must still expend Vitae as normal\u2014after all, the Sun remains a formidable foe without additional aid.<br /> <br /> <b>Defeat of Famine</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Dragon has defeated Famine, and it no longer poses a threat. A Dragon who has mastered this Coil is immune to frenzy caused by hunger. Though she may appear as a shriveled corpse, she retains complete self-control.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Unleashed</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u200b<br /> The potency of Vitae is significantly enhanced. Each point of Vitae now heals three points of bashing damage instead of one. Additionally, the Dragon receives a discount when activating Disciplines and Devotions, reducing the Vitae cost by one (to a minimum of one).<br /> <br /> <b>Rise of the Hemomancer</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> This Coil represents the peak of the Mystery of the Blood in empowering Vitae\u2019s properties. The Dragon has learned to refine his blood more quickly than others. Each dot of Blood Potency now costs 1 less experience point to purchase.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sample Scales of the Blood</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Living Host Extrapolation</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coil</b>: The Blood Bank<br /> <b>Procedure</b>: The Dragon extracts the blood of a human or Kindred subject and mix it with a specially prepared oil that preserves its properties. This mix can be inserted into an animal up to one month after the concoction is prepared. Draining all the animal blood and inserting the mixture in its place, the animal must have appropriate size to carry all the mixture.<br /> <b>Outcome</b>: The animal blood is treated as if it had human or Kindred blood for every point of Vitae -1 invested into the mixture, to a maximum of the animal size. Kindred blood still carries risk of Addiction and can cause Vinculum as normal, with the Regnant being the donor. This mixture is higly toxic, and the animal carrier will likely die in a couple hours after the infusion.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Reduction</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coil</b>: Rise of the Hemomancer<br /> <b>Procedure</b>: The Dragon fills a large bottle, prepared ahead of time with alchemical mixtures and boil it over the course of three hours.<br /> <b>Outcome</b>: For every three points of Vitae spilled into the mixture increase the mixtures\u2019s effective Blood Potency by one when determining if it is potent enough to wake up torpid Kindred. It only generate enough Vitae for a single dose and it uses this temporary Blood Potency for the attempt of waking up the Kindred in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-29-2025, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T19:41:21-07:00","id":1493092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493091-mystery-of-the-blood-2e-homebrew#post1493091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mind over Body</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> This Coil represents the furthest that the Mystery of the Blood has achieved in liberating the Dragon from the shackles of his need for blood. When the last Vitae from the Dragon is spent, instead of dropping into Torpor, he may remain awake for the remaining of the Scene. If he wishes to remain awake for more time than that, he needs to spend a point of Willpower. If he has no Willpower to spend, he will instantly fall into torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't fall into torpor just from running out of Vitae. If they try to wake up and don't have Vitae to spend on doing so or they end their with a track full of lethal damage after any reflexive expenditures of Vitae they might use to heal, they fall to torpor, but neither of those uses having no remaining Vitae left as the primary condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T03:58:58-07:00","id":1493103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493091-mystery-of-the-blood-2e-homebrew?p=1493092#post1493092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't fall into torpor just from running out of Vitae. If they try to wake up and don't have Vitae to spend on doing so or they end their with a track full of lethal damage after any reflexive expenditures of Vitae they might use to heal, they fall to torpor, but neither of those uses having no remaining Vitae left as the primary condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly played all this time as if a vampire somehow got to 0 Vitae in a scene he automaticaly fell into torpor. After some rereading i saw that you are right. I'm gonna have to change some things about the last power then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 09-15-2022, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T21:51:42-07:00","id":1494651,"title":"","content":"Had the idea in my head a while that nothing but a fresh infusioon of vitae can rise a revenany from torpor. but canr find it again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment